# Core and shell split

- Rust crates do not open windows, draw chrome, or import AppKit, Win32, or GTK.
- `llamp-ffi` is the only crate a shell links. The ABI is C: handles, POD, buffers, error codes. No Rust types across the boundary. cbindgen is the source of truth.
- Shells own windows, input, accessibility, and integer-scale blitting. They do not parse BMP or ZIP.
- The shell reads playback capability flags. It does not branch on provider name strings such as `"spotify"`.
- MusicKit, if it ships, stays in the Swift shell. It is Tier B. It does not feed the decode graph.
- Details: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
